# Normalize every text file to LF in the index and on checkout. Later lines win, so the narrower
# overrides below take precedence over this catch-all.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Pin the line ending per type rather than leaving it to auto-detection, and give git a C#-aware
# hunk header for .cs files.
*.cs text eol=lf diff=csharp
*.csproj text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.slnx text eol=lf

# Explicit so `* text=auto` cannot reclassify it.
*.png binary

# spec/openapi.raw.json is the pin. Its byte count and its sha256 are recorded in
# spec/PROVENANCE.json, so any end-of-line conversion on checkout makes the committed file disagree
# with its own record. Measured 2026-09-06: with core.autocrlf=true and no rule here, the
# checked-out file is 303,525 bytes rather than 291,311 and its sha256 is a655e7e9... rather than
# b1c0783a...
# Deliberately -text and not the binary macro. binary expands to -diff -merge -text and renders the
# spec delta as "Binary files differ", which destroys the reviewability a spec refresh depends on.
# linguist-generated drops the file from the language statistics and collapses it in GitHub diffs.
spec/openapi.raw.json -text linguist-generated

# spec/openapi.generated.json is what generator/preprocess_spec.py writes, and its sha256 is
# recorded in spec/PROVENANCE.json as generatedSpecSha256. Same reason as the rule above: the hash
# is computed over bytes that end-of-line conversion on checkout must not be allowed to rewrite.
spec/openapi.generated.json -text linguist-generated

# linguist-generated drops these from the language statistics and collapses them in GitHub diffs.
# src/Whisparr2.Net/ is openapi-generator output and .openapi-generator/FILES is its manifest of
# that output. Both are generated bulk that no reviewer reads line by line.
# Deliberately not the binary macro: it expands to -diff -merge -text, and -text would let a
# checkout rewrite the line endings that generatedTreeSha256 in spec/PROVENANCE.json is computed
# over.
src/Whisparr2.Net/** linguist-generated
.openapi-generator/FILES linguist-generated

# The one exception inside src/Whisparr2.Net/. The wide glob above matches the hand-owned
# Whisparr2.Net.csproj too, and that file is the one thing in that directory a reviewer must read
# line by line: its content is the difference between a working .snupkg and a dead one. Later
# lines win, so this narrower line releases it.
src/Whisparr2.Net/Whisparr2.Net.csproj -linguist-generated

# .openapi-generator/VERSION is left unmarked deliberately, and is not an oversight. It is one
# line holding the generator version, and a generator version bump is exactly the diff a reviewer
# wants shown, so collapsing it would remove the signal rather than reduce noise.
